      "title": "Troubleshooting HTTP 401 Errors and SSO Redirect Loops in Token Service",
      "content_summary": "This article addresses common authentication failures such as HTTP 401 errors, premature token expiration, and SSO redirect loops, providing guidance on identifying configuration issues and operator errors.",
      "content_body": "When users encounter HTTP 401 errors or SSO redirect loops, first verify that the Token Service configuration matches the supported identity provider settings. Check for operator errors such as incorrect client IDs or misconfigured redirect URIs in the SSO setup. If the issue persists, review logs for 'invalid token' messages which may indicate a token expiration handling bug requiring a product patch. For expired credentials or password reset link failures, ensure customers are educated on the correct reset workflow to avoid unnecessary support tickets. Finally, perform an access review to confirm that recent configuration changes have not inadvertently revoked valid sessions."
